\fBFileHandle (extends EventEmitter)\fR
A container for a descriptor tracked in `fds` and opened in the native layer. This class implements the Node.js `FileHandle` interface
.TP
\fBDEFAULT_ACCESS_MODE()\fR
Emitted when the file handle has been opened. Emitted when the file handle has been closed.
.TP
\fBfrom(id)\fR
Creates a `FileHandle` from a given `id` or `fd`
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string \\| number \\| FileHandle \\| object \\| FileSystemFileHandle; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIFileHandle\fR
.TP
\fBaccess(path, mode, options)\fR
Determines if access to `path` for `mode` is possible.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string; required)
.br
\fImode\fR (number; optional; default 0o666)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR
.TP
\fBopen(path, flags, mode, options)\fR
Asynchronously open a file.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIpath\fR (string \\| Buffer \\| URL; required)
.br
\fIflags\fR (string; optional; default 'r')
.br
\fImode\fR (string \\| number; optional; default 0o666)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<FileHandle>\fR
.TP
\fBopened()\fR
`true` if the `FileHandle` instance has been opened.
.TP
\fBopening()\fR
`true` if the `FileHandle` is opening.
.TP
\fBclosing()\fR
`true` if the `FileHandle` is closing.
